WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Charlie: Welcome to the sprint retrospective, team. Let's go over what went well and what we can improve. Alice, you want to start?

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.100
Alice: I think our velocity was great this sprint. Merging the new UI components early really helped QA get a head start.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.500
Bob: I agree. However, I want to call out that the database migration took much longer than expected. We almost missed the deployment window.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Charlie: Good point. What happened with the migration? I thought it was fully tested in staging.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:41.200
Bob: It was, but staging doesn't have the same data volume. Production has millions of rows, so adding an index locked the table for nearly 20 minutes.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Alice: That's a classic mistake. We should probably write a policy that all non-trivial schema changes need to use concurrent indexing.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:01.500
Bob: Yeah, I'll create an internal wiki page on how to safely run `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` in Postgres. I'll share it with the backend team.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Charlie: Let's make that a formal action item. Good takeaways, overall a very solid sprint. Let's keep it up!
